# Design commands — integrate, don’t paste

The following UI came from explicit design install commands. **Do not restyle locked component source files** unless the user explicitly asks.

Product pages must **wire** these via wrappers with Staz copy, CTAs, and surface tokens — never drop raw demos (portfolio hero, English “Simple Pricing”, keyboard playground) into the live landing or settings.

## Locked component sources

- `src/components/ui/glassmorphism-trust-hero.tsx` — use `StazGlassTrustHero` / `StazGlassWorkCard` in product; keep default `HeroSection` for `/demo` only
- `src/components/ui/modern-stunning-sign-in.tsx` / `modern-stunning-sign-in-demo.tsx`
- `src/components/ui/vintage-keyboard.tsx` — demo routes only unless product-framed
- `src/components/blocks/pricing.tsx` (Codehagen pricing block API + look)
- `src/components/spectrumui/animateddrawer.tsx` — account/upgrade drawers, not settings playground
- `src/shared/demo.tsx` (drawer demo icons)

## Allowed

- Wire via wrappers (`TrustSection`, `LandingPricing`, `AppShell`, settings plan block, demos)
- Pass product props (Staz plans, Hebrew copy, OTP handlers, open/close state)
- Fix build/type errors without changing the intended look of locked files

## Not allowed without explicit user request

- Restyling colors, spacing, typography, or animations inside locked files
- Replacing the command UI with a simplified/custom redesign inside locked files
- Pasting unmodified command demos into the main product surface
